    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a favorable slate today, with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Andy Pages** emerging as our top-tier plays. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** anchors the lineup with a robust 73.66 efficiency, benefiting from a soft matchup against Chandler and a prime #2 spot in the order. Similarly, **Andy Pages** draws a high-upside matchup against Sears; his 73.47 score is bolstered by a favorable wind-out condition and a significant platoon edge, making him a cornerstone for our production targets. **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo** also provide elite floor and upside against Lodolo, with both benefiting from favorable SP skill metrics despite the left-on-left dynamic.\n\nStrategic decisions for today\u2019s roster were defined by our strict efficiency floor and the scarcity of stolen bases. **Sam Antonacci** earns his start with a strong 62.96 score, largely driven by his favorable #1 spot and high xwOBA, which edges out the bench options. **Denzer Guzman** served as our toughest exclusion; while his 44.48 score suggests utility, he ultimately fell short because he lacks the elite sprint speed profile needed to justify a bump over our starting outfielders. Meanwhile, we continue to exercise caution with **Josh Lowe**, whose recent form and #9 spot in the lineup pushed him below our 40-point threshold, forcing him to the bench to preserve our precious game caps. \n\nManagers should monitor **Drake Baldwin** and **Dominic Smith** closely, as they face the toughest pitching opposition of the day in McLean. While both are in the lineup, their efficiency is depressed by the SP skill disadvantage. We remain vigilant regarding the health of our depth chart, as **Jordan Westburg** remains on the IL, further tightening our rotation constraints. We are effectively leaning into our high-order hitters today to maximize run production, prioritizing the speed-threat profiles of **Sam Antonacci** and **Andy Pages** to maintain our competitive edge in the SB category.",
